# Qt6 only. Five Qt5 package names used to live here and NONE of them exists in
# ::gentoo or ::bentoo any more, so every one of those lines was inert:
#
#   dev-qt/qtcore icu           -> absorbed by dev-qt/qtbase; `icu` is already set
#                                  on qtbase, both here and in base/package.use/core
#   dev-qt/qtprintsupport cups  -> absorbed by qtbase; `cups` already set on it below
#   dev-qt/qtquickcontrols2 widgets -> absorbed by dev-qt/qtdeclarative, where
#                                  `widgets` is on by default anyway
#   dev-qt/qtgui evdev jpeg eglfs   -> `evdev` and `eglfs` exist on qtbase but are
#                                  OFF; `jpeg` is not an IUSE of qtbase at all
#   dev-qt/qtsql mysql          -> `mysql` exists on qtbase and is OFF
#
# The last two are deliberately NOT migrated. Those flags have never actually been
# applied — the packages carrying them do not exist — so switching them on now
# would be a new product decision dressed as a cleanup, not a fix. If Qt needs
# MySQL, evdev or EGLFS, add them to the dev-qt/qtbase line in package.use/kde
# on purpose (lab, 2026-09-01, F18).

dev-qt/qtmultimedia qml
dev-qt/qtwebchannel qml
dev-qt/qtwebengine widgets
# `qml`, not `compositor`. dev-qt/qtwayland declares IUSE="gnome qml" -- there is
# no `compositor` flag, so the old line configured nothing. Meanwhile
# net-im/telegram-desktop (sets/comms, reached by every flavor) depends on
#     >=dev-qt/qtwayland-6.11:6[compositor(+),qml]
# where `(+)` forgives the missing `compositor` but `qml` is a real flag, OFF by
# default -- measured with this project's USE: qtwayland resolves as "-qml".
#
# NOT PROVEN to break a clean resolve: this build host already has qtwayland
# installed, so the dependency is satisfied here and the probe cannot exercise
# the case. Verify in step12-kde-resolve (2026-09-09).
dev-qt/qtwayland qml

# Python bindings for Qt, moved from the base on 2026-09-13. Neither package
# appears in the minimal plan, so configuring them there set nothing.
#
# On qtpy: the atom is LOWERCASE. The base spelled it `dev-python/QtPy` and
# Portage atoms are case-sensitive, so that line matched nothing for as long as
# it existed. `gui` and `printsupport` are IUSE defaults; only `svg` changes
# anything.
dev-python/qtpy gui printsupport svg
dev-python/pyqt6 qml
